# `helm package` output, and the subcharts it resolves. ADR-0725 has the release
# pipeline resolve this chart's eight dependencies at package time
# (`helm package chart -u`) rather than committing them, so `chart/charts/` is
# ignored the same way `yadgarhq/config` ignores it — this repository no longer
# differs from its siblings here. Both still land in the working tree the
# moment somebody runs `helm dependency update` or `helm package chart -u` by
# hand, which this repository's own test suite does.
*.tgz
chart/charts/

# WRITTEN BY `helm dependency update`, NEVER BY HAND — and per ADR-0725, not
# committed either. Nothing reads a committed copy: the release job always
# resolves fresh with `-u`, which regenerates this file and discards whatever
# git held, and `Chart.yaml` already pins exact versions with no ranges, so a
# committed lock would add nothing a reader could not already read there.
chart/Chart.lock

# Python bytecode, which `scripts/tests/` produces the first time it runs. Its
# suite is the only Python here and it is not packaged.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Scratch PR-body files agents write while reviewing. Ignored here, in the
# repository, instead of relying on a contributor's machine-wide git config —
# that cover exists on one machine and reaches no other clone, no CI, and no
# other contributor.
.local-review/
